{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "hydration-proof",
          "version": "1.2.3",
          "semanticVersion": "1.2.3",
          "informationUri": "https://hydration.jscrate.dev",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "HP1001",
              "name": "TextMismatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Text differs between server and client"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The server HTML contains different text than the browser rendered during hydration."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The server HTML contains different text than the browser rendered during hydration.\n\nHow to fix:\n- Render exactly the same text on the server and in the first client render.\n- Move browser-only or time-dependent values into useEffect, or compute them on the server and pass them down as props.\n\nhttps://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1001",
                "markdown": "The server HTML contains different text than the browser rendered during hydration.\n\n**How to fix**\n\n- Render exactly the same text on the server and in the first client render.\n- Move browser-only or time-dependent values into useEffect, or compute them on the server and pass them down as props.\n\n[Documentation](https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1001)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "hydration",
                  "react",
                  "dom-mismatch"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "HP1002",
              "name": "AttributeMismatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Attribute differs between server and client"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An attribute value in the server HTML differs from the value React rendered on the client. React does not patch attributes during hydration."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An attribute value in the server HTML differs from the value React rendered on the client. React does not patch attributes during hydration.\n\nHow to fix:\n- Compute the attribute from data that is identical on the server and the client.\n- React does not fix attributes during hydration, so users keep seeing the server value until the next update.\n\nhttps://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1002",
                "markdown": "An attribute value in the server HTML differs from the value React rendered on the client. React does not patch attributes during hydration.\n\n**How to fix**\n\n- Compute the attribute from data that is identical on the server and the client.\n- React does not fix attributes during hydration, so users keep seeing the server value until the next update.\n\n[Documentation](https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1002)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1002",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "hydration",
                  "react",
                  "dom-mismatch"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "HP1004",
              "name": "ClassMismatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Class name differs between server and client"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The class attribute rendered on the server differs from the className React renders on the client. The page keeps the server classes."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The class attribute rendered on the server differs from the className React renders on the client. The page keeps the server classes.\n\nHow to fix:\n- Make class names deterministic between server and client.\n- For themes, read the preference on the server (for example from a cookie) or set the class with a pre-hydration script and suppressHydrationWarning on that element.\n- For CSS-in-JS, set up the library's server style registry so class names are generated in the same order.\n\nhttps://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1004",
                "markdown": "The class attribute rendered on the server differs from the className React renders on the client. The page keeps the server classes.\n\n**How to fix**\n\n- Make class names deterministic between server and client.\n- For themes, read the preference on the server (for example from a cookie) or set the class with a pre-hydration script and suppressHydrationWarning on that element.\n- For CSS-in-JS, set up the library's server style registry so class names are generated in the same order.\n\n[Documentation](https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1004)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1004",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "hydration",
                  "react",
                  "dom-mismatch"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "HP1005",
              "name": "ExtraAttribute",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Attribute only present in the server HTML"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The server HTML has an attribute that React does not render on the client."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The server HTML has an attribute that React does not render on the client.\n\nHow to fix:\n- Remove the attribute from the server output or render it on the client too.\n\nhttps://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1005",
                "markdown": "The server HTML has an attribute that React does not render on the client.\n\n**How to fix**\n\n- Remove the attribute from the server output or render it on the client too.\n\n[Documentation](https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1005)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1005",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "hydration",
                  "react",
                  "dom-mismatch"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "HP1013",
              "name": "InnerHtmlMismatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "dangerouslySetInnerHTML differs between server and client"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The HTML injected with dangerouslySetInnerHTML differs between the server and the client. React does not patch it."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The HTML injected with dangerouslySetInnerHTML differs between the server and the client. React does not patch it.\n\nHow to fix:\n- Make the injected HTML identical on server and client, or render it after mount.\n\nhttps://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1013",
                "markdown": "The HTML injected with dangerouslySetInnerHTML differs between the server and the client. React does not patch it.\n\n**How to fix**\n\n- Make the injected HTML identical on server and client, or render it after mount.\n\n[Documentation](https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1013)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp1013",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "hydration",
                  "react",
                  "dom-mismatch"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "HP3003",
              "name": "DuplicateId",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Duplicate id attribute"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Several elements share the same id."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Several elements share the same id.\n\nHow to fix:\n- Give every element a unique id; generate ids for repeated components with useId.\n\nhttps://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp3003",
                "markdown": "Several elements share the same id.\n\n**How to fix**\n\n- Give every element a unique id; generate ids for repeated components with useId.\n\n[Documentation](https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp3003)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp3003",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "hydration",
                  "react",
                  "invalid-html"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "HP9004",
              "name": "NavigationFailed",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The page could not be loaded"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The browser could not navigate to the URL."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The browser could not navigate to the URL.\n\nHow to fix:\n- Check that the server is running and the URL is correct.\n\nhttps://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp9004",
                "markdown": "The browser could not navigate to the URL.\n\n**How to fix**\n\n- Check that the server is running and the URL is correct.\n\n[Documentation](https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp9004)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp9004",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "hydration",
                  "react",
                  "test-run"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "HP9010",
              "name": "UnexpectedRedirect",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The route redirected somewhere else"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The route ended on a different URL than requested (or than expectRedirect). A signed-in scenario that lands on a login page usually means its login did not work."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The route ended on a different URL than requested (or than expectRedirect). A signed-in scenario that lands on a login page usually means its login did not work.\n\nHow to fix:\n- If the redirect is intended, set expectRedirect on the route, or limit the route to the scenarios that can open it (scenario include/exclude).\n- For signed-in scenarios, check the login step or the storage state file.\n\nhttps://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp9010",
                "markdown": "The route ended on a different URL than requested (or than expectRedirect). A signed-in scenario that lands on a login page usually means its login did not work.\n\n**How to fix**\n\n- If the redirect is intended, set expectRedirect on the route, or limit the route to the scenarios that can open it (scenario include/exclude).\n- For signed-in scenarios, check the login step or the storage state file.\n\n[Documentation](https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp9010)"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://hydration.jscrate.dev/docs/issues/hp9010",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "hydration",
                  "react",
                  "test-run"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
